{"title":"2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db1bf40a4a8119b9a32be2b01d22c20a12225e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> is a straight angle.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/f/73f97006d3242f96548a656c467e650833fbd1e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 100 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 140 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 50 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 120 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 320$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the diagram, we see that the measures of angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f575aad1d3f0e4d9224e9a8233e21c321c1bc72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/b/58b18468b4a258225435497f9a38d791b720649e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RQS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> sum up to the measure of angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c587b0c1e5de0bde79b9d8c36913c16dee04d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />. This means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/0/1d09a0f670c171f8664c3555e03ac99c410e09d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{\\circ} + 40^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/497f29c93ea9f5a3f1851e6c03f53f63043fe58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ} - 40^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/4589ff5e8d10f30f56bab07d38ef719c41f4ddf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 140}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Gauss (Gra